######
#
# Atsdoc: the text processor for .atxt files
#
######

An .atxt file is a text with placeholders, #name(args) (or #name{text}, or #name),
and blocks of ATS code between a line that starts with %{ and a line that starts with
%} (also %{^ ... as in ATS1). atsdoc translates it into an ATS2 program (--outcode)
and the text (stdout, or --outdata) where each placeholder is replaced by #__tokN$
(the program binds __tokN to the value of the call and puts it in theAtextMap). The
program is linked with libatsdoc (../../libatsdoc) and prints the text with the
placeholders replaced by the values.

    usage: atsdoc <command> ... <command>
      -i filenames | --input filenames     the input files (stdin if there is none)
      -oc filename | --outcode filename    where the program goes (stdout)
      -od filename | --outdata filename    where the text goes (stdout)
      --prefix string                      the prefix of the names __tokN
      -h | --help                          the usage

The file names are printed as they are given in the messages (position and error).
The options and their quirks are those of the ATS1 version of atsdoc (a file name
after -i that starts with a hyphen is an option once a file was given, -h counts as an
input, ...); the messages and the exit status are the same.

atsdoc is written in ATS2 without GC (the modules of ../../src for the lexical buffer,
the positions and the file names, linked from libatsopt.a); ATS1 is not needed.
HATS/ holds the helper files that the .atxt files include (postiatsatxt.hats,
xhtmlatxt.hats, docbookatxt.hats, pats2xhtmlatxt.hats, pats2dbookatxt.hats), ported to ATS2.
The differences from the ATS1 version are listed in src/PORTING.md ("atsdoc and libatsdoc").

######

Building:

  make                  # BUILD/atsdoc, copied to $(PATSHOME)/bin/atsdoc; libatsdoc.a, copied
                        # to $(PATSHOME)/ccomp/atslib/lib (libatsopt.a is built if it is missing)
  make check            # typechecks the files
  make test             # TEST/: the md5 suite (python3; see TEST/Makefile)
  make -f ../../Makefile_devl bin_atsdoc    # the same, from the root (not part of [all])

######
